  "answer": "The goal was not met. Only two of the five cases were confirmed, and only one of them is a rear-end of the lead car. On 0e899dd3, moving the lead pickup 1 s earlier and slowing it to 0.5x, with 100 ms planner delay, made the ego hit its rear in every run (S16). But the ego took over only about 0.5 s before contact, with roughly 6 m of gap, so triage could not say whether the policy was at fault. On 19f339ba, a 1 s earlier shift at the recorded speed with 100 ms delay also failed every run (S22), but the lead car was not involved: the policy braked hard for no reason and drifted left into a car in the next lane. The only other failures were on 096988dd (S5) and 19f339ba at zero delay (S23). Both are the same kind of left drift into a passing car, and with only one to three runs at each setting they are hints, not confirmed rates. Five scenes never failed at any setting tried. No failure was flagged as a possible simulator artifact.",
